
  The other half of my recommendation is a reordering: [1mtasks come before notifications.[0m There's nothing to be notified
  [3mabout[0m yet. I'd rather design "tasks with a change-event seam" as the first project, then notifications as the second,
  than design a notification system against a task model we're inventing in our heads as we go.

  That said, "tasks they care about" is a real hint that you're picturing more than one person. If shared tasks are
  actually the point of the app — not a someday-maybe — say so, and the whole calculus changes.

